 "text": "Hi, how are you doing these days? Keep it simple. Welcome everyone with coffee in the backyard, or down the park if it' dry. A piece of cake cake, or a box of macarons, is beautiful hostess. Your partner if they want to, or a dear friend. A friend keeps it celebration, though. A box of old photos is lovely. Start with everyone full eyes closed, then open them for the pledge. It counts without words. In the garden, the idea of it being for you both together matters much more than words. Keep it short so voices don't hurt, maybe five minutes. And let everyone hold a small memento if they have one. Then",
